<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Game management · Nister Admin</title><link rel="icon" href="/assets/nister-browser-icon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com"><link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin><link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:wght@400;600;700&family=Sora:wght@300;400;500;600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/spin.css?v=11"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/spin-admin.css?v=11"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/spin-portal.css?v=1"><link rel="stylesheet" href="/assets/premium.css?v=20260603-premium9"><script src="/assets/spin-admin.js?v=11" defer></script></head>
<body class="spin-body spin-admin admin-console"><a class="skip" href="#admin-content">Skip to administration</a><div id="spin-admin" class="wrap" data-csrf="<?=spin_html($csrf)?>"><header class="topbar"><a class="brand-lockup" href="/admin/"><div class="mark" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div><div><h1 class="brand">Nister Admin</h1><div class="muted">Flight management</div></div></a><nav class="actions" aria-label="Administration"><a class="btn" href="/admin/">WISP console ↗</a><button class="btn" id="refresh-admin" type="button">Refresh</button></nav></header>
<main class="admin-main" id="admin-content"><div class="admin-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow gold">FLIGHT · OPERATIONS</span><h1>Game management.</h1><p>Control future play. Preserve every obligation.</p></div><div class="admin-state"><span id="admin-state" class="live-badge">Loading</span><button id="ghost-control" class="ghost-button" type="button">Activate Ghost Mode</button></div></div><p class="notice" id="admin-message" role="status" hidden></p><p class="notice" id="launch-notice" hidden>A game manager must log in to authorize play. Server readiness, audit signing, and explicit restoration or activation are required. The default authorization window is 48 hours after the latest successful game-manager login.</p>
<div class="admin-metrics" id="overview-metrics"></div>
<nav class="admin-tabs" aria-label="Game management sections"><button type="button" data-tab="overview" aria-current="page">Overview</button><button type="button" data-tab="pool">Prize pool</button><button type="button" data-tab="rules">Game rules</button><button type="button" data-tab="players">Players &amp; wallets</button><button type="button" data-tab="analytics">Analytics</button><button type="button" data-tab="ghost">Ghost Mode</button><button type="button" data-tab="audit">Security &amp; audit</button></nav>
<section data-panel="overview"><div class="admin-columns"><article class="admin-card"><div class="card-title"><h2>Operational pulse</h2><span class="eyebrow">PERSISTENT SERVER STATE</span></div><div id="pulse" class="definition-list"></div><p>Credits remain redeemable while the game is paused or ghosted. Takeoff holds the stake atomically; collection or automatic completion settles the accepted flight.</p><div class="button-row"><button type="button" class="secondary-btn" data-state="PAUSED">Pause game</button><button type="button" class="secondary-btn" data-state="ACTIVE">Activate game</button></div></article><article class="admin-card"><h2>Financial reconciliation</h2><p>Verify pool movements, cash debits, network-credit balances, balanced journals, and the tamper-evident receipt chain.</p><button class="secondary-btn" id="reconcile" type="button">Run reconciliation</button><pre id="reconcile-result" aria-live="polite">Not evaluated in this browser session.</pre><p>Delivery cost and displaced revenue are estimates. Winnings are credited to the regular customer wallet. The prize pool is a separate budget.</p></article></div><h2>Recent transitions</h2><div id="overview-events"></div></section>
<section data-panel="pool" hidden><div class="admin-columns"><article class="admin-card"><h2>Adjust the prize pool</h2><p>Pool adjustments change an internal results budget. They do not create a customer cash deposit. Decreases cannot exceed the available pool.</p><form id="pool-form" class="admin-form"><label for="pool-delta">Signed adjustment (GHS)</label><input id="pool-delta" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="100.00 or -50.00" required><button class="primary-btn" type="submit">Review pool adjustment →</button></form></article><article class="admin-card"><h2>Total-return exposure</h2><div id="exposure"></div><p>The ceiling covers the entire return, including returned stake. Active flights reserve their payout envelopes. There is no pool-dependent stake rejection; an unfunded envelope can return zero.</p></article></div><h2>Pool movements</h2><label for="movement-filter">Movement type</label> <select id="movement-filter"><option value="all">All movements</option><option value="manual">Manual adjustments</option><option value="game">Game settlements</option></select><div id="pool-table"></div></section>
<section data-panel="rules" hidden><article class="admin-card"><div class="card-title"><h2>Future flight configuration</h2><span id="config-version" class="live-badge"></span></div><p>The selected minimum edge is charged at opening. Later ordinary movements preserve their current expected value, including zero events and clipped upward moves. Every version is immutable; accepted flights keep their version and reserved total-return ceiling. The total return never exceeds 2x the stake or 10% of the pool. The opening return is derived from your selected minimum expected edge and zero-event setting. New flights open below the stake. Direction probabilities are calculated from the actual up/down amounts to preserve the stopping-strategy bound. A 2x peak lasts at most one second before a one-pesewa dip. These checks apply on the server.</p><form id="rules-form" class="admin-form rules-grid"><input type="hidden" name="movement_model" value="balanced">
<label>Minimum expected house edge (%)<input id="min-house-edge" name="min_house_edge_ppm" type="number" min="0" max="99.9999" step="0.0001" required><small>A minimum expected margin across stopping strategies, not guaranteed profit on individual rounds.</small></label><p id="edge-summary" class="edge-summary" aria-live="polite"></p>
<label>Zero-event setting (basis points)<input name="zero_bps" type="number" min="0" max="10000" required><small>Included in the opening edge. Later zero events are compensated by surviving returns; their probability reduces near the ceiling.</small></label>
<label>Minimum movement (% of current return)<input name="min_move_pct" type="number" min="1" max="100" required></label><label>Maximum movement (% of current return)<input name="max_move_pct" type="number" min="1" max="100" required></label>
<label>Pool ceiling (basis points)<input name="pool_bps" type="number" min="1" max="1000" required><small>1,000 = 10%, applied to the ENTIRE return.</small></label><label>Minimum stake (pesewas)<input name="min_stake_cents" type="number" min="1" required></label>
<label>Movements per flight<input name="steps" type="number" min="4" max="20" required></label><label>Movement duration (milliseconds)<input name="step_ms" type="number" min="1000" max="3000" required></label>
<label>Optional daily stake limit (0 = none)<input name="daily_stake_cents" type="number" min="0" required></label><label>Optional daily loss limit (0 = none)<input name="daily_loss_cents" type="number" min="0" required></label><label>Minimum flight interval (seconds)<input name="interval_seconds" type="number" min="0" max="3600" required></label>
<label>Movement distribution<select name="distribution"><option value="uniform">Uniform whole percentages</option><option value="weighted">Explicitly weighted</option></select></label><label>Movement weights (JSON percentage : weight)<textarea name="weights" rows="3" spellcheck="false"></textarea><small>Uniform uses []. Weighted requires both range endpoints.</small></label><button class="primary-btn" type="submit">Review &amp; activate new version</button></form></article>
<article class="admin-card"><h2>Return estimates by stopping strategy</h2><form id="preview-form" class="inline-form"><label for="preview-stake">Actual stake (GHS)</label><input id="preview-stake" inputmode="decimal" value="10.00" required><button class="secondary-btn" type="submit">Calculate</button></form><div id="preview-result" aria-live="polite"></div><p>Previews the current form, including unsaved changes, against the pool after active reservations. Previewing does not change the active rules. The opening expectation and edge bound are exact model calculations. Automatic-finish calibration estimates only the small expected cost of one-pesewa ceiling rebounds; the strategy table separately simulates actual payouts with standard errors. Neither estimate promises winning odds. A player's stopping strategy affects results.</p></article><h2>Flight configuration history</h2><div id="config-history"></div></section>
<section data-panel="players" hidden><article class="admin-card"><h2>Customer records</h2><form id="search-form" class="inline-form"><label for="player-search">Canonical account number</label><input id="player-search" inputmode="tel" placeholder="233xxxxxxxxx"><button class="secondary-btn" type="submit">Search / clear</button></form><p>Existing WISP accounts and their regular wallet balances. A gameplay restriction affects Flight only.</p></article><div id="players-table"></div><div class="admin-columns"><article class="admin-card"><h2>Game access review</h2><form id="player-form" class="admin-form"><label>Account<input name="msisdn" pattern="233[0-9]{9}" required></label><label>Action<select name="review_action"><option value="identity">Optional age review</option><option value="restrict">Restrict gameplay</option><option value="allow">Remove game restriction</option></select></label><label>Date of birth (identity review only)<input name="birth_date" type="date"></label><label>External verification reference<input name="verification_ref" maxlength="128" autocomplete="off"></label><button class="primary-btn" type="submit">Review customer decision →</button></form></article><article class="admin-card"><h2>Traceable credit correction</h2><p>Creates a compensating network-credit journal. Existing outcomes and receipts cannot be edited. Use a dispute reference in the reason; cash corrections stay in the WISP billing console.</p><form id="correction-form" class="admin-form"><label>Account<input name="msisdn" pattern="233[0-9]{9}" required></label><label>Signed correction (GHS)<input name="amount" inputmode="decimal" required></label><button class="primary-btn" type="submit">Review credit correction →</button></form></article></div><h2>Deposits &amp; monetary ledger</h2><div id="cash-table"></div><h2>Stakes &amp; outcomes</h2><div id="spins-table"></div><h2>Legacy network-credit ledger</h2><div id="credits-table"></div><h2>Credit-funded internet purchases</h2><div id="redemptions-table"></div></section>
<section data-panel="analytics" hidden><article class="admin-card"><div class="card-title"><h2>Flight stakes &amp; returns</h2><select id="period" aria-label="Analytics period"><option value="day">Daily</option><option value="week">Weekly (UTC Monday)</option><option value="month">Monthly</option></select></div><div class="performance-chart" id="performance-chart" role="img" aria-label="Recent daily stake volumes, also available in the table below"></div><div id="daily-table"></div><p>Profit rates reflect settled flights, including the effect of player stopping decisions. The chart covers up to the latest 90 active days.</p></article><div class="admin-columns"><article class="admin-card"><h2>Flight outcomes</h2><div id="distribution-table"></div></article><article class="admin-card"><h2>Network-credit economics</h2><div id="credit-economics"></div><p>Estimated delivery cost uses the current configured cost ratio. Possible displaced revenue is a face-value upper bound, not a measured causal loss.</p></article></div></section>
<section data-panel="ghost" hidden><div class="admin-columns"><article class="admin-card"><h2>Visibility &amp; availability</h2><div id="ghost-details" class="definition-list"></div><p>Ghost Mode blocks new flights. Accepted flights retain collection and automatic settlement, including after refresh. Receipts, pool movements and audit access remain available. A later administrator login does not restore the game.</p><div class="button-row"><button type="button" class="ghost-button" data-state="GHOSTED">Activate Ghost Mode</button><button type="button" class="secondary-btn" data-state="RESTORE">Restore Game</button><button type="button" class="secondary-btn" data-state="PAUSED">Pause</button><button type="button" class="secondary-btn" data-state="ACTIVE">Activate</button></div></article><article class="admin-card"><h2>Persistent inactivity watchdog</h2><p>Only a successful interactive password login by an authorised game manager resets the clock. Customer logins, API traffic, token refreshes and jobs do not qualify. Availability checks enforce the deadline even between watchdog runs.</p><form id="threshold-form" class="admin-form"><label for="threshold-hours">Inactivity threshold (hours)</label><input id="threshold-hours" type="number" min="1" max="168" value="48" required><button type="submit" class="primary-btn">Review threshold change →</button></form><p>Lowering the threshold may ghost the game immediately. The watchdog is always enabled.</p></article></div><h2>State transition history</h2><div id="transition-table"></div></section>
<section data-panel="audit" hidden><article class="admin-card"><h2>Security boundaries</h2><p>Game manager allowlist + existing WISP administrator session are required for every privileged mutation. Every operation needs an idempotency key and an audit reason. No administrator can choose or replace an individual outcome.</p><p>Audit records form a keyed HMAC chain. The watchdog checks the chain against materialised balances and settled receipts. Keep signing keys outside the database and export audit heads to your independent monitoring archive.</p><button class="secondary-btn" id="export-audit" type="button">Export this audit page</button></article><div id="audit-table"></div></section>
<div class="pagination"><button type="button" id="previous-page" class="secondary-btn">Previous records</button><span id="page-number">Page 1</span><button type="button" id="next-page" class="secondary-btn">Next records</button></div></main>
<dialog class="game-dialog" id="admin-confirm" aria-labelledby="admin-confirm-title"><form method="dialog"><button class="dialog-close" aria-label="Cancel change">×</button></form><span class="eyebrow gold">PRIVILEGED ACTION</span><h2 id="admin-confirm-title">Confirm the change.</h2><pre id="admin-change-preview"></pre><form id="admin-confirm-form" class="admin-form"><label for="admin-reason">Reason / approval / dispute reference</label><textarea id="admin-reason" minlength="8" maxlength="500" required></textarea><button class="primary-btn" type="submit" id="admin-apply">Confirm &amp; record change</button><p id="admin-confirm-message" role="status"></p></form></dialog></div></body></html>
